description:
pkix-path/src/lib.rs:1585, 1737, 1783, 1902, 1917

Five separate 'use x509_cert::ext::pkix::...' statements appear inside curly-brace blocks within chain_walk's per-cert loop body:

    { use x509_cert::ext::pkix::certpolicy::CertificatePolicies; ... }
    { use x509_cert::ext::pkix::PolicyConstraints; ... }
    { use x509_cert::ext::pkix::PolicyMappings; ... }
    { use x509_cert::ext::pkix::PolicyConstraints; ... }  // repeated
    { use x509_cert::ext::pkix::InhibitAnyPolicy; ... }

PolicyConstraints appears twice (lines 1737 and 1902).  In Rust 2021 there is no namespace-pollution reason to scope these inside blocks; they do not conflict with anything at the module level.  Block-scoped 'use' is appropriate when a name would shadow an outer name — that is not the case here.

The block-scoped pattern reads as if these types are somehow exotic or risky to import globally.  Moving them to the module top (or at least to the top of chain_walk) makes the function's dependencies visible at a glance and eliminates the repeated PolicyConstraints import.
